course: dictionary
lesson: 1405
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and card is a good example. To choose the right meaning, read the words around it, which is its context. «Borrowing books from the public library is free, and a parent can help you get your own library card.» Library tells you this card is for borrowing books, so it means a small plastic card that shows who you are.
explain: «The referee's word is final: a yellow card is a warning, a red card sends a player off.» Warning, sends off and player show that card means something given in a game, not paper or plastic. The same word, a different meaning, because of the clues around it.
explain: Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence? Then put your meaning in place of the word and check that the sentence still makes sense. If you are not sure, a dictionary lists every meaning of the word, so you can compare them.
fact: Card can have several meanings, so check the context before you choose one.
fact: «Card» can mean a small flat piece of stiff paper with a picture, such as a trading card.
fact: «Card» can mean a folded paper with a picture and a message, such as a birthday card.
fact: «Card» can mean one of a pack used in games, such as playing cards; a full pack has 52.
fact: «Card» can mean a small plastic card for paying or showing who you are, such as a bank card or library card.
exercise: «Borrowing books from the public library is free, and a parent can help you get your own library card.» What kind of card is a library card? | A folded paper with a picture and a message | A small flat piece of stiff paper with a picture | *A small plastic card for paying or showing who you are | One of a pack used in games
exercise: «The referee's word is final: a yellow card is a warning, a red card sends a player off.» In this sentence, what does card mean? | *A warning given to a player in a game | A folded paper with a picture | A small plastic card for paying | A pack of playing cards
exercise: Sam has 3 packs with 8 cards in each. How many cards does he have altogether? | 11 | *24 | 38 | 83
test: «Zara got a gift card for a game she does not even play.» What is the gift card? | One of a pack used in games | A small flat piece of stiff paper with a picture | *A small plastic card for paying in a shop | A folded paper with a picture and a message
test: Mia shuffled the deck of 52 cards before the game started. What does card mean here? | A small plastic card for showing who you are | *One of a pack used in games | A small flat piece of stiff paper with a picture | A folded paper with a picture
exam: Which meaning of card fits best in «Grandma sent me a birthday card with a loving message inside»? | *A folded paper with a picture and a message | One of a pack used in games | A small plastic card for paying | A warning given in a game
